        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Norbert Holm, Erwin Rommel\n- Roles: General, Field Marshal, Chief of Operations, Military Theorist\n- Organizations: Wehrmacht, Nazi Germany\n- Events: World War II, 20 July plot\n\nFacts:\n- Erwin Rommel was born on 15 November 1891 and died on 14 October 1944.\n- Norbert Holm was born on 16 December 1895 and died on 3 June 1962.\n- Erwin Rommel was a German general and military theorist.\n- Erwin Rommel, popularly known as the Desert Fox, served as a field marshal in the Wehrmacht of Nazi Germany during World War II.\n- Norbert Holm was a general in the Wehrmacht of Nazi Germany during World War II.\n- Following the 20 July plot, Norbert Holm was arrested on 16 September 1944 and was later demoted because of his association as Chief of Operations with Field Marshal Erwin Rommel.",
